<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44279" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sĭlus</span></b> , i, or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sīlo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, m.
		1. silus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Roman surname</i>, esp. of the gens Sergia.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> M. Sergius Orata
			Silus, <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 2, 70,
			285</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			M. Sergius Silus, <i><span class="en">Liv. 32, 27, 7</span></i>; 
			 Eckhel. D. N. 5, p. 306.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> Domitius Silus, <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 15,
				59 <i>fin.</i></span></i> al.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> In the form Silo: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Arruntius Silo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 48, 19, 27</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Plin. 11, 37, 59, §
		158</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
